From 0b33aacd0a87025dff7782059fd30b8a4c3d4fd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:49:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07189/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-8: re-enable
 induction -- blocked by a different gate, not the harness disable

Answers the last open hypothesis from REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-6/5699-7: is
one of the OTHER disabled production features (induction, frame-
change scorer, goal-bias, go-explore archive) load-bearing for a
first level-up on g50t/sk48/cd82?

--induction added to the CLI: constructs a real LocalGGUFProposer
(Qwen3.5-9B-MTP, the frozen live-submission defaults) on a dedicated
port (8930, distinct from the SGE router's own gemma-4-12B-it server
on 8929) instead of the _NoOpInductionProposer stub, and stops
setting CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_INDUCTION=1 (checked via sys.argv before
that env-var line runs, since it's set at module scope before main()
would otherwise parse it).

Real run (SGE + induction, budget=46, all 3 games): still
real_max_level_observed=0 -- but induction_attempts_not_skipped=0
too. Direct inspection of each game's real induction_attempts log
(E3AgentPolicy's own record) shows every attempt was skipped with
"hidden_state_trust_below_threshold", NOT "disabled_by_env" --
confirming the harness disable really was bypassed, and induction
hit a genuine, separate, pre-existing production safety gate
instead. Traced to source: all 3 games are members of
HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS (coincidentally, not by deliberate selection),
which requires select_trusted_world_model's trust_pass
(heldout_change_consistency >= threshold) before any LLM induction
call. All 3 games showed heldout_change_consistency at or near zero
after only 25 observed transitions from a cold budget=46 start, so
the gate never clears.

Honest framing: this is not "induction was tried and didn't help" --
it's "induction was never actually invoked, for a specific, traced
reason distinct from every prior null in this investigation." Two
new follow-ups, not a third re-run of these 3 games: (1) does a
larger budget let the trust gate clear naturally (a different
question than REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-7's "does budget change the level
outcome" -- that run had induction disabled throughout); (2) test a
game NOT in HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS, where this gate doesn't apply and
induction would actually fire from the first stall.

3 new unit tests (induction disabled by default passes the no-op
stub; induction enabled passes a real, correctly-configured
LocalGGUFProposer; spec-declaration). Spec: REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-8 with
its own scenario.

